# Vulnerabilities in the deployer image that are genuinely blocked on an
# upstream fix, not something we can patch ourselves. Everything here is
# baked into gcr.io/cloud-marketplace-tools/k8s/deployer_helm's own
# `kubectl` and `helm` binaries (Google's own build, not ours) or is a
# transitive dependency with no published fixed release yet. Any NEW
# finding not listed here still fails the scan.
#
# Verified 2026-09-11 with `trivy image` directly against the built
# deployer image — see chart repo GKE_LIVE_TESTING.md and
# https://github.com/GoogleCloudPlatform/marketplace-k8s-app-tools/issues/688
# for the go1.26.5 stdlib finding, which affects every Marketplace deployer
# built from this base image, not just ours.

# stdlib (go1.26.5, baked into Google's own kubectl and helm binaries;
# fixed in 1.25.13/1.26.6/1.27.0-rc.3 — Google hasn't republished the base
# image with a patched toolchain yet)
CVE-2026-33818
CVE-2026-39821
CVE-2026-46600
CVE-2026-56853
CVE-2026-56858
CVE-2026-56859
CVE-2026-56860
CVE-2026-56862

# golang.org/x/net / golang.org/x/text (kubectl v1.36, Google's own binary)
CVE-2026-25681
CVE-2026-27136
CVE-2026-33814
CVE-2026-56852

# golang.org/x/crypto and oras-go (helm CLI, Google's own binary) — same
# CVE-2026-56854 also remains in our own nk binary: nkeys v0.4.16 (the
# latest published release) only pulls golang.org/x/crypto v0.52.0; the
# fix needs 0.55.0, not yet available in any nkeys release.
CVE-2026-56854
CVE-2026-50163
